  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new stream camera has a bug that will cause the camera to interfere with itself when placed high off the ground.  I have a large Rat avatar that I use to place the stream camera high up and lock it to world positioning.  When I do this, the camera lens will block itself.  If the camera lens is set to transparent, the video has a blue haze.  If it is set to solid, the video is blocked completely.  If it set it to invisible it works fine (and I'm using this as a workaround).  So far, this only seems to happen when using a camera high off the ground, or perhaps using a very large avatar to set the camera in position.  I'm not sure which, though I think it is height related.  PS.  I really like the new camera.",
